=== A. SEC FAQ Example 27-1 (market buy 3000 sh; NBBO 25.30 x 25.60 at receipt) ===
fill  400 @ 25.50: buy effective spread = 2 x (25.50 - 25.45) = 0.10
fill 1000 @ 25.55: buy effective spread = 2 x (25.55 - 25.45) = 0.20
fill 1600 @ 25.60: buy effective spread = 2 x (25.60 - 25.45) = 0.30
share-weighted effective spread = 0.2400 USD  (FAQ: 0.10/0.20/0.30 weighted by 400/1000/1600)
=== B. FAQ Example 38-1 share-weighted average percentage price improvement ===
net price improvement = 2.00 USD; sum(mid x shares) = 35,092; pct = 0.005699%
=== C. toy report coverage, then signed effective spread (synthetic) ===
excluded  o4: ('special_handling', 'fill-or-kill')
excluded  o5: ('special_handling', 'non-IOC pegged')
excluded  o6: ('directed_order_at_receiving_broker', True)
excluded  o7: ('nbb_or_nbo_outside_luld_bands', True)
excluded  o8: ('received_outside_regular_hours', True)
excluded  o9: ('nbbo_crossed_30s_or_more', True)
excluded o10: ('halt', '<5 min before halt (receipt), outstanding')
excluded o13: ('halt', '<5 min before halt (first executable), outstanding')
covered  o11 (NMLO): received pre-open, later executable in regular hours
covered  o12 (NMLO): received during a halt, executable after resumption
covered  o14 (NMLO): received 2 min before halt, first executable only after resumption
report coverage: 6 orders; ES computed for 3 market/marketable orders (1000 sh)
avg signed ES = -0.0100 USD; avg mid = 35.02 USD; avg % effective spread = -2.8555 bps
(toy mean of per-order bps = -1.9992 bps -- a different statistic, do not call it the 605 number)
if you (wrongly) ignore the exclusions: 23.13 bps
negative here = fills on the customer's side of the mid in THIS toy sample; not a negative fee, not a promise.
lesson assumption: half-spread 5 bps -> compare ORDER OF MAGNITUDE only; 605 = reporter aggregate,
covered orders; it is not your own fill cost and not a broker ranking.
